#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log_base

#% text
# `log_base(b, x)` gives the logarithm of `x` to base `b`, exact when `x` is a power of the integer `b`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
log_base(2, 1024)
#% output
#= 10

#% cell
log_base(10, 1000)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
log_base(3, 7)
#% output
#= log(7)/log(3)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Numerical values:

#% cell
n(log_base(3, 7))
#% output
#= 1.7712437491614221

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A machine real goes through `log(x)/log(b)`, so the last digit can be off:

#% cell
log_base(10, 0.001)
#% output
#= -2.9999999999999996

#% text
# A reciprocal power is not yet recognised as exact:

#% cell
log_base(2, 1/8)
#% output
#= -1*log(8)/log(2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `log2`, `log10`
